.TH CTPOOL_TIMED_SUBMIT 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ctpool_timed_submit \- submit a task with a relative timeout
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadpool.h>

ccol_retval_t ctpool_timed_submit(ctpool pool,
                                  void (*fn)(void *),
                                  void *arg,
                                  void (*on_complete)(void *),
                                  struct timespec *timeout);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Identical to ctpool_submit except that for bounded queues it waits at
most timeout for a free slot. The timeout is a relative duration;
internally it is converted to an absolute deadline using CLOCK_REALTIME.

Passing NULL as timeout is equivalent to ctpool_try_submit (no waiting).
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
pool         Thread pool handle
fn           Task function (must not be NULL)
arg          Passed to fn and on_complete (may be NULL)
on_complete  Called after fn returns (may be NULL)
timeout      Relative duration to wait (NULL = do not wait)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success           - task enqueued.
ccol_invalid_args      - pool is CTPOOL_INVALID or a stale/already-destroyed handle, or fn is NULL.
ccol_not_enough_memory - task struct allocation failed.
ccol_not_permitted     - pool is shutting down.
ccol_container_full    - NULL timeout and queue is full.
ccol_timed_out         - timeout elapsed before a slot became free.
ccol_unexpected_failure - clock_gettime or pthread_cond_timedwait
                          returned an unexpected error.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_submit (3),
.BR ctpool_try_submit (3)
